    "category": "Orthopedics: Surgical Goals and Outcomes",
    "questionText": "A 13-year-old skeletally immature boy has a right thoracic curve of 56 degrees that has progressed despite bracing. He is scheduled for posterior spinal fusion with modern segmental instrumentation and bone grafting. His parents ask what the operation is realistically expected to accomplish and how reliable it is. Which statement is most accurate?",
