    "questionText": "An 8-year-old girl with open triradiate cartilages undergoes isolated posterior spinal fusion with instrumentation for a rapidly progressive curve. Two years later she returns with worsening trunk asymmetry. Imaging shows a solid posterior fusion mass with intact hardware and no lucency, yet the rib prominence is markedly worse and the sagittal contour has changed. Which mechanism best explains this outcome?",
